  "term": "clinically relevant behavior",
  "definition": "In this study, clinically relevant behavior refers to child behavior problems severe enough to fall in the concerning range on a behavior checklist. It was used for internalizing or externalizing problems when the child’s score reached the study’s cutoff for a behavior problem.",
